---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

// Static site: no forms, no newsletter, no accounts, no cookies, no Google
// Analytics, no Brevo. Only Vercel (hosting) and Matomo (cookieless,
// IP-anonymised analytics) are used, so only they are named here.
const updated = '25 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="No cookies and no forms. Learn how nzebra.eu uses Vercel hosting and cookieless Matomo analytics, and how to contact us about your data."
>
  <div class="news-wrap">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Header variant="light" />
      <div class="uui-page-padding-3">
        <div class="uui-container-large-3">
          <div class="uui-padding-vertical-xhuge-5">
            <div class="uui-max-width-large-3">
              <h1 class="uui-heading-large">Privacy policy</h1>
              <div class="uui-space-small-3"></div>
              <article class="uui-text-rich-text w-richtext">
                <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

                <h3>Who is responsible for this website</h3>
                <p>
                  This website (<a href="https://nzebra.eu">www.nzebra.eu</a>) presents the work of
                  the nZEBRA project, co-funded by the European Union under the Erasmus+ programme.
                  The website is run by Three o'clock, the data controller for any personal data
                  processed through it. You can reach us at
                  <a href="mailto:hello@threeoclock.eu">hello@threeoclock.eu</a>.
                </p>

                <h3>What data we collect</h3>
                <p>
                  This is an information-only website: it has no accounts, no login, no contact
                  forms and no newsletter sign-up. We do not ask you for any personal data, there
                  are no forms to submit it through, and we do not set any cookies.
                </p>
                <p>
                  As with any website, our hosting provider automatically processes the basic
                  technical information needed to deliver pages to you (such as your IP address and
                  browser type) in its server logs. We also measure anonymous, aggregate usage
                  statistics as described below.
                </p>

                <h3>Hosting</h3>
                <p>
                  The website is hosted by Vercel, which processes the technical request data above
                  on our behalf to serve the site and protect it against abuse. See Vercel's privacy
                  notice at
                  <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>.
                </p>

                <h3>Analytics</h3>
                <p>To understand which pages are useful, we use Matomo in a privacy-friendly way. Matomo:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>does not set any cookies and does not track you across websites;</li>
                  <li>anonymises your IP address, so you are not personally identified;</li>
                  <li>produces only aggregate statistics such as page views and referring sites.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                  Because the data is anonymous and no cookies are used, this analytics does not
                  require a consent banner.
                </p>

                <h3>Documents</h3>
                <p>
                  Course materials and project documents (PDF and Office files) are served directly
                  from this website. Downloading them does not require you to provide any information.
                </p>

                <h3>External links</h3>
                <p>
                  Some pages link to external websites (for example partner institutions or EU
                  resources). Those sites have their own privacy policies, which we do not control.
                </p>

                <h3>Your data protection rights</h3>
                <p>
                  Under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) you have rights of access,
                  rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability regarding your
                  personal data. Because this website does not collect personal data that identifies
                  you, we normally hold nothing to act on — but you can contact us at any time at
                  <a href="mailto:hello@threeoclock.eu">hello@threeoclock.eu</a> with a request or
                  question.
                </p>

                <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
                <p>
                  We may update this policy if the services behind the website change. The date at
                  the top shows when it was last revised.
                </p>

                <h3>Supervisory authority</h3>
                <p>
                  If you believe your data protection rights have not been respected, you have the
                  right to lodge a complaint with your national data protection authority.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
